<title>POLAND: Polish broad money rises 1.6 pct in February -NBP.</title>
<headline>Polish broad money rises 1.6 pct in February -NBP.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's broad money rose by 2.17 billion zlotys, or 1.6 percent, in February to 138.34 billion after a 0.1 percent rise in January, preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Broad money supply grew 2.46 billion or 1.8 percent in the January-February period.  </p>
<p> BROAD POLISH MONEY		    FEB 97    JAN 97	FEB 96</p>
<p> Month/month change (pct)	     1.6     0.1		2.5</p>
<p> Money in bln zlotys		  138.34  136.17(136.04) 108.06</p>
<p> Foreign currency (in bln PLN)     24.57   24.23 (24.26)  21.29</p>
<p> National currency		    113.77  111.94(111.79)  86.77</p>
<p> Cash in circulation		   23.45   22.78 (22.77)  20.19</p>
<p> Lending to non-financial sector   85.29   83.40 (83.33)  58.37</p>
<p>NOTE - revised figures in brackets. -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
